# DA–DE Kurss full audit (mandatory pattern)

When tasked with **DA Kurss linguistic audit**, follow `docs_and_rules/DA-KURSS-FULL-AUDIT-TASK.md` exactly.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Auditor:** GPT-5.6 Luna — full linguistic review; regex-only is not sufficient.
2. **READ-ONLY:** Do not modify production (`data/da/`, `www/data/da/`, `languages/da/`).
3. **DE = STRICT READ-ONLY:** Never edit `de` fields or DE dialogue in lessons.
4. **LV = MASTER for structure only:** IDs, order, section types, card counts, renderer logic, pedagogy — compare against `data/courseLessons.js`. **Do not copy LV text as DA.**
5. **Coverage:** All 21 lessons + 6 extra topics + L1–7 training cards + Kurss UI keys = 100%.
6. **Check:** spelling, grammar, semantics, naturalness, consistency, fictional person names, LV/CS/BS/EN remnants, placeholders.
7. **Findings format:** Finding ID, lesson/path, DE_CURRENT, DA_CURRENT, PROPOSED_DA, severity, category, rationale.
8. **Verdict:** PASS only with 0 findings (all severities) + DE changes 0 + technical PASS. Else NEEDS OWNER REVIEW.

## After audit (automatic)

When findings remain, auto-generate OWNER review pack (A1/A2 pattern):

- `reports/da-kurss-owner-review-GITHUB.md`
- `reports/da-kurss-owner-decisions*.md`
- `reports/da-kurss-owner-accepted*.md`

Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Production files

- `data/da/courseLessons.js` — main audit target
- `data/da/courseTrainingCards.js` — L1–7 cards
- `languages/da/ui.js` — `kurss.*` section labels

## Validators (run in addition to Luna)

```bash
node scripts/validate-kurss.js --lang=da
node scripts/verify-da-de-compliance.js
```

